<title>FRANCE: Chirac says French 97 deficit around 3.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Chirac says French 97 deficit around 3.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>French President Jacques Chirac said on Monday that France's 1997 public sector deficit was running at about 3.5 percent of gross domestic product.</p>
<p>&quot;We have reached a current situation which must be about 3.5 percent (of GDP),&quot; Chirac said in a live television interview, adding that it was within France's reach to achieve the three percent goal set by the Maastricht treaty to qualify for a single European currency.</p>
</text>
